WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.432
Pandas json normalize can flatten nested JSON into columns.

00:00:04.432 --> 00:00:08.642
Nested keys such as metrics heart rate and metrics steps become analytical fields.

00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:14.667
Notice what happens when a key exists in only one record.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.377
The other record receives a missing value.

00:00:17.377 --> 00:00:23.147
Flattening solves the structural problem, but it creates new quality questions about missingness, units,

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:29.822
and field meaning. Technical normalization is only the beginning of analytical understanding.

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:36.512
A useful project question is: what preparation step is required before analysis can even begin?

00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:39.707
A relational table may be ready for profiling, JSON may need flattening,

00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:45.632
and free text may need NLP or another extraction step.

00:00:45.632 --> 00:00:49.317
The form of the data changes the engineering path, but it does not by itself tell us whether

00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:52.718
the data is high quality.
